# Keep the build context small and the image correct.
#
# Without this file `docker build` uploads node_modules/ and dist/ as build context — tens of
# thousands of files, painfully slow from a Windows host — and, because the Dockerfile does
# `COPY . /app/` before `npm install`, the host's node_modules is copied INTO the image. Native
# modules built for the host platform then sit in a Linux image, which is a correctness problem
# as well as a size one.
node_modules
dist
tmp
.angular
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
docs
*.md
